# API design (Google AIP) — always on

Canonical hub: [Google API Design Guide](https://cloud.google.com/apis/design). Eventsliner map: [docs/21-platform-standards.md](docs/21-platform-standards.md).

Building or changing `/api/**` without this is **forbidden**.

## MUST

- Versioned under `/api/v1/`.
- Resource-oriented URLs (`/orgs/{org}/events/{event}/…`), not RPC-ish verbs in paths.
- Errors via `errorJson()` / `withApiContext()` from `@/lib/api/response` (AIP-193 JSON: `code` HTTP, `status` rpc Code, `reason` ErrorInfo, `details[]`).
- List methods: support `pageSize` + `pageToken`, return `nextPageToken` (`@/lib/api/pagination`). Legacy `limit`/`offset` only as aliases.
- JSON fields `lowerCamelCase`.
- Create → `201` with the resource. Delete → `200`/`204` consistently.
- Check **permission before existence** for private resources (403 vs 404).
- Idempotent webhooks; verify signatures before side effects.
- Include `X-Request-Id` (handled by `json` / `withApiContext`).

## MUST NOT

- Invent a second error shape (`{ error: "string" }` or ad-hoc codes).
- Return stack traces or internal SQL to clients.
- Put secrets or PII in error `metadata` beyond what the caller already knows.
- Break existing clients that read `error.message` / form `fields` without a migration path.

